hello everybody and welcome again to a  new presentation of a competition that  we have recently published  this time we are selecting  highly  qualified professionals in the field of  space and  defense i say highly quite qualified  professionals because indeed we offer  these competitions on quite advanced  levels  grade 87 and 9  in both the fields of defense industry  and space  you can apply for only one field and one  grade  now if you apply for the 89 grade which  is the highest grade  and  if the selection board things that you  do not qualify for the 89 grade  they can reassign you to the 87 grade  if you are okay with that so you can  indicate in your application form where  you  allow the selection board to do so  if you wish so  we have published on our website as  usual an infographic this one that you  see here which gives you in the blink of  an eye an overview of this competition  the eligibility criteria the different  steps of the competition and then  eventually the number of people that  we're looking to select this time  what i'll do in this presentation is  walk you through these different steps  with a bit of more detail to it  so first of all the eligibility criteria  for an ad7 competition you need at least  either a master degree plus six years of  experience in the field  or a bachelor degree with seven years of  experience  for 89 you need a master plus 10 years  or a bachelor degree plus 11 years of  experience  his experience must be of course in the  field the field of defense or space as  explained below there a couple of  examples defense includes defense  research and development procurement  defense  industrial policy  and then for the space domain you see  for instance space r d  economics law satellite navigation these  kind of things  then there's also of course a language  criterium  you need to speak at least two eu  languages  one of which must be english as you can  see below  one language you must master on level c1  so you need a thorough  language knowledge there  and your second language must be at  least level b2 meaning a satisfactory  level okay  how does the selection procedure look  like this there's always different steps  everything starts of course with an  application and a registration on our  website  a first selection is done through what  we call a talent screener i will explain  in a minute what that means the ones  getting through this first stage are  invited to the second stage which is an  assessment center and there we test a  set of skills and competencies  if you are successful you are what we  call a laureate and you can be recruited  by mainly  the commission director general for  defense industry and space we call it dg  defes  all right  so let's  dive into  the detail of these different steps  to apply you first of all need an epso  account  if you do not have an exo account yet  you can create one easily on our website  if you do have one do not create a  second one because you can only have one  account  to  take part in any competition that you  want  you have to apply on our website on the  home page  www.eu  careers.eu you will find a direct link  to this competition  you can apply in any of the 24 languages  apart from the talent screener part that  part you have to fill in english  you have to validate your application at  the latest on the 19th of july that's a  deadline for this competition  so by that date you can go in and out of  your application you know save it go  back complete it a bit more go back when  you want  but you have to validate it at the  latest on the 19th of july  once that is done we start selecting and  the first stage is this typical  talent screener phase which is basically  a set of  six to nine questions that you have to  answer when you fill out your  application  and we basically  um assess your qualifications here we  see we look at the degrees you have we  look at the professional experience you  have in these domains  and we give you scores for the answers  to these different questions  the candidates with the highest scores  are then invited to the second stage  which is the assessment center  in the assessment center i said we will  assess a number of skills and  competencies  firstly we test your reasoning skills we  test your verbal numerical and abstract  reading skills  in which language well not in english  but in the other language that you have  mentioned to us when you applied  you need a combined pass mark of 20 out  of 40 combined so meaning in theory you  can't fail for  one of these reasoning skills tests if  you if you want as long as you make up  for them uh in the other tests  i advise you strongly to  train this you can do so by checking out  our sample tests on the website  because first of all there is the level  of difficulty of these questions  but secondly there is also a time factor  involved  so you have to be able to solve these  questions under time pressure and by  training this you get better at this so  have a look on our sample tests to train  you for this phase  once you pass this phase once you have  the pass mark out of 20 out of 14  minimum you go to the next phase  when you go to the next phase you start  from zero again so the score you get  here in this reading skills test does  not count towards the overall score at  the end  so secondly we will test  a set of eight general competencies and  we do so  uh through two tests both of these tests  are to be conducted in english  there is an oral presentation to be done  which will test four competencies  and there is a situational competency  based interview during which we test  four more competencies you see though  in this slide here  the whole test or both of these tests  are to be conducted in english  again you need a combined pass mark at  least 40 out of 80.  currently um or i mean the the score you  get here  will count towards the end okay so it is  important to score well on each of these  competencies um that you are tested in  secondly uh we test a set of field  related competencies  again through two different tests  there's an interview and there's a  written test where we test  your competencies and knowledge uh in  the field  you need at least 25 out of 50 both  times and again your score here does  count towards the overall score  the best ones scoring end up on the list  of successful candidates and those are  the ones that will be recruited by this  dg deficit as said in the beginning you  see the numbers of laureates requested  here so we need 32 successful candidates  in the 87  grade for defense 16 for 89 and so on so  in total we're looking to recruit 100  people so it's quite a big competition  actually  so  i invite you to  apply  please do read the notice of competition  carefully this is the legal document  containing all information on the duties  the eligibility criteria the different  steps of the competition in detail  you'll find most of the of your answers  of any question you might have in this  notice of competition so do read  carefully  if you would have more questions to this  competition you can always reach out to  us  via our web form on the website  and we can then come back to you with  any answer  that's it for now good luck to this  competition and see you around next time  bye
 

